WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.300
While Lysandre's plan to create his ideal world moves ahead,

2
00:00:06.366 --> 00:00:09.166
Clemont is attempting to take back Prism Tower,

3
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:14.266
Serena and Mairin are rescuing Chespie, and Bonnie is chasing after Squishy.

4
00:00:14.566 --> 00:00:17.700
All of our heroes are valiantly doing what they can.

5
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.566
As for Ash and Greninja, they have broken free from Lysandre's restraints

6
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.700
and are about to unleash their counterattack alongside Alain.

7
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.333
All right, Noivern, use Boomburst!

8
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.400
Now, Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

9
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.900
Outnumbering me is completely unimportant.

10
00:00:42.966 --> 00:00:44.566
Use Hyper Beam.

11
00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:48.166
Now, Dragon Tail!

12
00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:56.633
Noivern!

13
00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:00.466
Cha... Hawlucha?

14
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:04.966
Thanks a lot, Noivern.

15
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.933
Use Dragon Claw.

16
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.966
Hawlucha, use High Jump Kick.

17
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:19.400
Catch it, quick!

18
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.833
Hawlucha!

19
00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.566
You were great, Hawlucha.

20
00:01:29.766 --> 00:01:31.233
We'll take it from here.

21
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.666
This power... the power of Mega Evolution...

22
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.366
it only happens during battle.

23
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.433
It's a kind of battle instinct.

24
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.733
Something Pokémon forgot after being in constant contact with humans.

25
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.166
But when a Pokémon unleashes its battle instinct...

26
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.333
that's when it gains Mega Evolution power.

27
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.400
Stop it. You've got it wrong.

28
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:59.233
Only the victor can prove that he's not wrong, Alain.

29
00:01:59.766 --> 00:02:02.100
Now, Hyper Beam!

30
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.066
- Wait!
- Let me go.

31
00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:10.800
I've gotta get to Squishy.

32
00:02:10.866 --> 00:02:13.800
- Then what will you do?
- I've gotta save Squishy.

33
00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.800
I promised I wouldn't let it go ever, ever again.

34
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:21.166
- Let go.
- No. Bonnie.

35
00:02:58.466 --> 00:03:01.000
The right hero for the right job.

36
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.333
I found the right code.

37
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.966
- Who's there?
- I'm the Lumiose Gym Leader Clemont.

38
00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.633
And I'm the substitute Gym Leader Clembot.

39
00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:23.366
- What do you see?
- I'm scanning now.

40
00:03:25.766 --> 00:03:27.900
There are three of them, one further back.

41
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.200
I detect the same elements in their device as contained within the red Zygarde.

42
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.300
Maybe it's their control system.

43
00:03:35.366 --> 00:03:38.033
It's possible I could infiltrate their system

44
00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.900
- and stop it from functioning.
- Good.

45
00:03:40.433 --> 00:03:42.033
Use Electric Terrain!

46
00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:50.533
- Clembot, now's your chance.
- Right.

47
00:03:51.366 --> 00:03:52.800
What's all the ruckus?

48
00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.400
Hm?

49
00:03:55.466 --> 00:03:56.566
Well, well.

50
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:59.666
I see we have some uninvited guests.

51
00:04:00.266 --> 00:04:02.733
What are Bryony and the others doing?

52
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.433
You're controlling Zygarde with that control system.

53
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.433
True. It's one of my greatest inventions.

54
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.166
Things that control Pokémon, destroy cities,

55
00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:15.533
bring pain and misfortune to people don't count as inventions.

56
00:04:17.233 --> 00:04:18.533
What do you know?

57
00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.666
Real inventions are things that help people and Pokémon.

58
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.933
You think that will change the world?

59
00:04:28.966 --> 00:04:30.833
I believe it with all my heart.

60
00:04:30.966 --> 00:04:33.100
All right, Crobat, use Air Slash!

61
00:04:33.166 --> 00:04:34.566
Malamar, Psycho Cut.

62
00:04:37.666 --> 00:04:39.266
Bunnelby, use Mud Shot.

63
00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:41.066
Chespin, use Pin Missile.

64
00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.333
It looks like we have visitors.

65
00:04:54.566 --> 00:04:56.133
Someone's there.

66
00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.833
Ice Shard, go!

67
00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.333
Braixen, ready?

68
00:05:06.166 --> 00:05:07.900
Weavile, use Ice Shard.

69
00:05:08.533 --> 00:05:10.633
Use Flamethrower!

70
00:05:14.233 --> 00:05:15.433
She's amazing.

71
00:05:15.866 --> 00:05:17.166
Icy Wind, go!

72
00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:26.533
What was that?

73
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.433
Hey, look.

74
00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.433
Steven.

75
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.466
You mean Steven the champion?

76
00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.500
Use Meteor Mash!

77
00:05:46.866 --> 00:05:48.933
The Hoenn champion, Steven.

78
00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:53.900
Lysandre fooled me. But he fooled the whole world, after all.

79
00:05:53.966 --> 00:05:56.900
Oh, please. Deception has nothing to do with it.

80
00:05:56.966 --> 00:06:00.133
This is a great undertaking to recreate the world.

81
00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.366
Hm. Great undertaking, huh?

82
00:06:02.433 --> 00:06:05.700
The smart thing to do would be to side with us.

83
00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.700
Really? You think so?

84
00:06:09.766 --> 00:06:13.866
Battle me, and you're gonna find out the hard way you're no match.

85
00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.866
- Steven!
- We're happy you're here.

86
00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:20.900
I'm glad I came to check things before going to Prism Tower.

87
00:06:20.966 --> 00:06:24.400
Mairin's Chespin is inside... and the Giant Rock.

88
00:06:24.866 --> 00:06:25.766
Right.

89
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.266
It really is the Hoenn champion.

90
00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:29.766
Get that babe on tape.

91
00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.300
Cool your jets.

92
00:06:31.733 --> 00:06:32.766
Wobbuffet!

93
00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.633
- I'll handle this. Get going.
- Right.

94
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.900
Weavile, now, Ice Shard!

95
00:06:43.733 --> 00:06:44.800
Use Dark Pulse!

96
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.333
Flash Cannon!

97
00:06:51.366 --> 00:06:52.200
This way.

98
00:06:52.266 --> 00:06:55.333
We're inside the evil Team Flare's secret base,

99
00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.966
but we will continue coverage, even when faced with danger.

100
00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:08.266
Are you all right?

101
00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.233
Come on.

102
00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:13.733
You need prior approval for an interview.

103
00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:16.466
- Why, you.
- Who do think you are?

104
00:07:16.533 --> 00:07:18.733
Your glasses are choking your brain.

105
00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:25.300
- Team Rocket.
- You keep appearing like a bad dream.

106
00:07:26.366 --> 00:07:29.200
- Get going.
- Go and save your precious Pokémon.

107
00:07:31.166 --> 00:07:34.133
Any enemy of our enemy is a good buddy to us.

108
00:07:34.566 --> 00:07:38.233
We have no intention of handing this world over to you thugs.

109
00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.833
It's a Team Rocket world.

110
00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.900
- Wait.
- It's the boss's world.

111
00:07:41.966 --> 00:07:44.400
Stop the babble. It's so boring.

112
00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.533
I know you are. Gourgeist, use Seed Bomb.

113
00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:49.166
Inkay, use Psybeam.

114
00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.666
Drapion, Sludge Bomb!

115
00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:58.966
We'd better hurry.

116
00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:03.700
Thunder Punch, now!

117
00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:08.200
Dragon Pulse!

118
00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.533
Use Hyper Beam!

119
00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.533
All right. Goodra, return.

120
00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:27.100
Oh, done so soon?

121
00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.533
No way.

122
00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.500
I never quit until it's over. I think you called that fighting spirit.

123
00:08:34.733 --> 00:08:37.400
But there's a lot more to a Pokémon's strength than that.

124
00:08:37.466 --> 00:08:39.233
I learned that on my journey.

125
00:08:39.299 --> 00:08:43.433
My Pokémon's strength and my strength come from believing in each other

126
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.500
and caring for each other more than anything else.

127
00:08:50.833 --> 00:08:53.433
If you don't understand that, we'll show you.

128
00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.466
Talonflame, now. Use Flame Charge.

129
00:08:56.533 --> 00:08:58.266
And, Greninja, you use Cut.

130
00:09:00.566 --> 00:09:02.000
Use Stone Edge.

131
00:09:04.733 --> 00:09:05.800
Catch them!

132
00:09:09.166 --> 00:09:10.966
- Above you!
- Dragon Tail!

133
00:09:19.766 --> 00:09:21.900
You were great. Thanks, Talonflame.

134
00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.066
What's wrong?

135
00:09:28.633 --> 00:09:32.366
With that big talk of yours, is that all you can come up with?

136
00:09:32.433 --> 00:09:33.766
Well then, this is it.

137
00:09:34.066 --> 00:09:35.500
Use Hyper Beam!

138
00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.200
Huh?

139
00:09:43.466 --> 00:09:45.366
- Hey, you're--
- Malva?

140
00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:48.366
Time for all this to end. Right now.

141
00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.933
Malva. What's the meaning of this?

142
00:09:51.366 --> 00:09:55.366
It's really simple. I'm putting my complete trust in these kids.

143
00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.400
Who's that Pokémon?

144
00:10:04.033 --> 00:10:05.933
It's Crobat.

145
00:10:10.866 --> 00:10:13.366
I know this world is hardly perfect.

146
00:10:13.666 --> 00:10:14.566
Far from it.

147
00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.633
Then why are you getting in my way?

148
00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.066
Because I saw them.

149
00:10:20.766 --> 00:10:23.566
Changing the world isn't about destroying it.

150
00:10:23.833 --> 00:10:27.600
- And people like them are proof of that.
- Then let me ask you.

151
00:10:27.833 --> 00:10:30.500
These children, who are destined to lose,

152
00:10:30.666 --> 00:10:33.433
what kind of world are they capable of making?

153
00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.833
- They haven't lost yet, have they?
- Hm?

154
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.866
Changing the world is not something they can do by themselves.

155
00:10:40.933 --> 00:10:45.233
But if adults like us offer a hand, things can change for the better.

156
00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.833
The possibilities are real, and I want to see that.

157
00:10:50.466 --> 00:10:52.366
Our conversation is through.

158
00:10:52.933 --> 00:10:55.466
You've wasted enough of my precious time.

159
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.233
Gyarados, incinerate, now!

160
00:11:00.833 --> 00:11:03.233
Greninja, Water Shuriken!

161
00:11:10.166 --> 00:11:11.066
Now, look.

162
00:11:11.366 --> 00:11:14.233
You may not like this world much, so what?

163
00:11:14.666 --> 00:11:17.566
It belongs to people and Pokémon. Everyone.

164
00:11:18.033 --> 00:11:20.833
Your plan to recreate the world, all that talk,

165
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.800
you have no right to say any of that.

166
00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:27.633
There are people meeting new people all the time.

167
00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.700
People making their dreams come true.

168
00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.800
People just getting started on their journeys.

169
00:11:33.233 --> 00:11:37.700
People who are healing from old wounds. Everyone's got their own tomorrow.

170
00:11:38.433 --> 00:11:42.100
And you have no right to take their tomorrows away from them.

171
00:11:43.133 --> 00:11:44.333
That's why we fight.

172
00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:47.433
My Pokémon and I are fighting for their tomorrows.

173
00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.766
Sounds like the future Ash talks about is pretty bright.

174
00:11:56.033 --> 00:11:58.033
How naïve can you get?

175
00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:02.800
You sound just like me back in the days when I was naïve.

176
00:12:05.066 --> 00:12:07.200
Thank goodness. Chespie's safe.

177
00:12:07.633 --> 00:12:11.000
- Let's take Chespie back to my lab.
- Thanks, professor.

178
00:12:18.666 --> 00:12:20.066
They don't give up.

179
00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.000
- How's Chespie?
- It's fine. See?

180
00:12:24.733 --> 00:12:26.000
Thank goodness.

181
00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.966
How do we get ourselves out of this situation?

182
00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.633
Now, come on. You don't really wanna get hurt, do you?

183
00:12:38.066 --> 00:12:39.133
It's Steven.

184
00:12:45.633 --> 00:12:46.833
Thanks, Blaziken.

185
00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.333
Squishy.

186
00:12:50.766 --> 00:12:54.533
- Are you sure about this?
- I know Squishy will understand.

187
00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:56.100
Please believe me.

188
00:12:56.666 --> 00:12:58.866
Squishy, it's fine now.

189
00:12:58.933 --> 00:13:00.800
It's me. Bonnie.

190
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:01.933
Can you see me?

191
00:13:02.433 --> 00:13:05.433
Squishy, you don't wanna do this, do you?

192
00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.033
I know you don't.

193
00:13:12.633 --> 00:13:14.066
No! Blaziken Mask.

194
00:13:16.433 --> 00:13:17.333
Squishy.

195
00:13:26.033 --> 00:13:29.366
♪ Squishy, Squishy ♪

196
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.766
♪ You're, oh, so very soft ♪

197
00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:37.466
♪ Squishy, Squishy ♪

198
00:13:37.966 --> 00:13:41.133
♪ You're, oh, so pretty green ♪

199
00:13:42.466 --> 00:13:44.900
♪ Squishy, Squishy ♪

200
00:13:46.066 --> 00:13:48.833
♪ The cutest I've ever seen ♪

201
00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:54.833
♪ You're happy sleeping in my bag Squishy ♪

202
00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.166
Dedenne.

203
00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:06.000
♪ Squishy, Squishy ♪

204
00:14:06.966 --> 00:14:09.300
♪ You're oh, so very soft ♪

205
00:14:09.733 --> 00:14:11.933
♪ Squishy, Squishy ♪

206
00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.633
♪ You're oh, so pretty green ♪

207
00:14:15.433 --> 00:14:18.000
♪ Squishy, Squishy ♪

208
00:14:18.466 --> 00:14:21.133
♪ The cutest I've ever seen ♪

209
00:14:21.533 --> 00:14:26.533
♪ You're happy sleeping in my bag Squishy ♪

210
00:14:27.533 --> 00:14:31.566
♪ How I wish I understood Where you come from ♪

211
00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:36.833
♪ And the way you get All your food from the sun ♪

212
00:14:37.333 --> 00:14:42.233
♪ Mysterious Squishy, how I love you so ♪

213
00:14:42.433 --> 00:14:46.933
♪ Oh, please, won't you please Tell me some more ♪

214
00:14:47.566 --> 00:14:52.700
♪ Squishy and me nuzzling cheeks ♪

215
00:14:52.933 --> 00:14:57.500
♪ Best friends forever, we're so happy ♪

216
00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:02.833
♪ I promise I'll never leave Squishy ♪

217
00:15:02.966 --> 00:15:07.700
♪ Sweet little Squishy Here's my song for you ♪

218
00:15:08.066 --> 00:15:11.200
♪ I'll never leave Squishy ♪

219
00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.600
♪ My sweet Squishy, that's you ♪

220
00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:38.800
Squishy.

221
00:15:39.366 --> 00:15:40.566
You heard me.

222
00:15:40.833 --> 00:15:42.300
You heard my voice.

223
00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:44.566
You heard my voice.

224
00:15:51.833 --> 00:15:53.100
Squishy!

225
00:16:06.066 --> 00:16:07.100
What's happening?

226
00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:09.333
Amazing. Zygarde's splitting.

227
00:16:09.866 --> 00:16:11.666
What's going on, Xerosic?

228
00:16:12.033 --> 00:16:15.933
Look, I'm too busy to deal with that. I'm battling an intruder.

229
00:16:16.533 --> 00:16:17.833
Battling an intruder?

230
00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.500
- It's the Lumiose Gym Leader.
- Clemont.

231
00:16:22.233 --> 00:16:24.000
You're all so useless.

232
00:16:36.733 --> 00:16:37.766
Squishy.

233
00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.633
You're okay now.

234
00:16:41.833 --> 00:16:45.100
Chespin, use Pin Missile. Bunnelby, use Mud Shot.

235
00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.700
Return, you two.

236
00:16:55.966 --> 00:16:57.666
-Oh, now what?

237
00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:00.733
I've done it. I've infiltrated the system.

238
00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.833
- What are you doing?!
- Activate the system.

239
00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:04.733
Roger.

240
00:17:10.233 --> 00:17:13.133
- That worked out quite nicely.
- Who knew?

241
00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.099
It sure came in handy, though.

242
00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:17.300
It's my invention, after all.

243
00:17:19.366 --> 00:17:22.466
Synchronizing you with the system. Shutting it all down.

244
00:17:24.466 --> 00:17:25.633
Hold on. What?

245
00:17:26.433 --> 00:17:29.633
If we force it to shut down, it will heavily stress the system.

246
00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:34.800
And because I'm synchronized with it, my main memory will be completely erased.

247
00:17:34.866 --> 00:17:36.533
I won't remember a thing.

248
00:17:36.966 --> 00:17:39.200
- Nothing?
- Right.

249
00:17:39.266 --> 00:17:41.566
Hold on a minute. I can't do that.

250
00:17:42.633 --> 00:17:45.400
But if we don't, this crisis will never end.

251
00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:50.933
You're Clemont, the leader of the Lumiose Gym.

252
00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:53.933
A kind and generous gym leader.

253
00:17:54.466 --> 00:17:56.100
Always thinking of others.

254
00:17:56.166 --> 00:17:58.766
Considering the good of many over the one.

255
00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:03.566
You know what you must do, so do it.

256
00:18:12.933 --> 00:18:14.800
I know. I know.

257
00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:16.800
I have to.

258
00:18:18.233 --> 00:18:20.700
Or I won't be able to help anyone.

259
00:18:35.733 --> 00:18:38.233
You are the one who can save the world.

260
00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:41.466
You once suggested to me that we learn together.

261
00:18:43.466 --> 00:18:46.300
And I want to keep on learning. Right, Clembot?

262
00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.800
Well put, sir.

263
00:18:49.966 --> 00:18:53.066
It made me happy. Thank you.

264
00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.666
Oh, Clembot.

265
00:18:56.966 --> 00:18:58.600
I'm so happy I know you.

266
00:18:59.533 --> 00:19:02.833
Thanks. And I'm so glad that you created me.

267
00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:04.300
You're brilliant.

268
00:19:05.433 --> 00:19:06.566
Oh, Clembot.

269
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.033
What's wrong?

270
00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:09.366
There. The other one has been freed, too.

271
00:20:10.366 --> 00:20:13.166
- Did Clemont do that?
- I bet.

272
00:20:13.466 --> 00:20:16.566
Lysandre, you guys just lost big-time.

273
00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:22.833
I have to say there seems to be no limit to how much you fools can entertain me.

274
00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:33.400
Zygarde is finally free from Team Flare's control

275
00:20:33.466 --> 00:20:35.233
thanks to Clemont and Bonnie.

276
00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:39.766
But will Ash and Alain be able to protect the world and its future from Lysandre?

277
00:20:39.833 --> 00:20:44.666
The Team Flare incident that shook Kalos takes an unexpected turn,

278
00:20:44.733 --> 00:20:47.300
as the journey continues.
